headers {
  X-WAGW-Origin: {{originSecret}}
  ~CF-Access-Client-Id: {{cfClientId}}
  ~CF-Access-Client-Secret: {{cfClientSecret}}
}

auth {
  mode: none
}

docs {
  # WA_GW API — Bruno collection

  Set the **Local** environment (top-right), then fill `adminToken` (from your
  `.env`). Create an agent key with **Admin > Keys > Create key** — its
  post-response script stores the plaintext into `agentKey` automatically.

  Auth model (what you are testing):
  - Agent routes (`/v1/chats`, `/v1/messages`, `/v1/send`, `/v1/drafts`, ...)
    require `Authorization: Bearer {{agentKey}}` — enforced per-endpoint by the
    `current_auth` dependency.
  - Admin routes (`/v1/admin/*`) require `Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}`
    — enforced by the router-level `require_admin` dependency (plus a Cloudflare
    Access JWT when `CF_ACCESS_ENABLED`).
  - `/mcp` requires the agent key, checked by `MCPAuthMiddleware`.
  - `/v1/health` and the `/admin/approvals` HTML shell are intentionally open.

  The **Auth checks** folder demonstrates rejection (401/403). When testing the
  public origin, set `originSecret` (and, for admin through Access, enable the
  two `CF-Access-*` collection headers).
}
